# Camera & scenes

- **AppScope** (prefab via `VContainerSettings`, DontDestroyOnLoad): `AppContext`, `ShellService`, `SaveService`, `InputService`, `AudioService`, EventSystem, `LoadingScreen` (overlay canvas, also the task list). No camera, no world.
- **MainMenu:** own Main Camera (+ `StudioListener`, no Brain), splash/menu canvases, `PressAnyKeyScreen` / `MainMenuScreen`.
- **Run scenes** (`Game`, `Blockout/GameBlockout`): the shared `#GameRun` prefab (scope, session, cameras with Brain + `StudioListener`, city, agents, `WorldAudio`, HUD) plus the scene's own `@Dressing` (lights, volume, environment, pyramid model). `$Dev` / `ScenarioEditor` lives only on GameBlockout. World audio deps come from `GameLifetimeScope`, not `Find*ObjectByType`.
- `#GameRun` holds no art. Building and worker models come from the `VisualSet` on `SceneDressing`; catalog building prefabs are shells without a model.
- `Game` never references `Blockout/`. The blockout only overrides on its own instance; editing `GameRun.prefab` edits both scenes.
- Exactly one `StudioListener` at a time. Scenes are never loaded on top of each other with two cameras.

# Audio

- `AudioService` (process) owns banks, music, snapshots, UI sound. It never reads ECS; Game's `SimPauseAudioBridge` feeds it the pause.
- FMOD paths, banks and buses live in `Content/Audio/AudioCatalog` — no `event:/` strings in code. FMOD `Load Banks` is None: `Core` loads with the process, `GameWorld` is acquired by `GameEntry` and released on teardown.

